  "label": "general internet audience",
  "description": "The meme is designed for a broad, general internet audience familiar with viral meme formats and cynical humor. It targets viewers who may be exposed to or create content that uses irony, dark humor, or absurdist framing to comment on global issues, often with a tone of detachment or moral relativism. The meme’s appeal lies in its provocative juxtaposition — using a child’s suffering as a punchline — which resonates with audiences who enjoy shock value, satire, or commentary that challenges conventional empathy. The target community includes individuals who may be indifferent to or apathetic toward global humanitarian crises, or who use such memes to justify inaction by framing suffering as 'part of the system' rather than a systemic failure.",
